## 3.1. Characterization of $N H_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs
SEM and TEM were employed for characterization of the morphology of the $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs. As seen in Fig. 1A and Fig. 1B, the as-prepared $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs showed cuboid-like shape with a mean length of $200\pm30\mathrm{nm}$ and a width of $130\pm35\mathrm{{nm}}$ . EDS mapping (Fig. S1) and XPS analysis (Fig. S2) confirmed the presence of C, Cu, $\mathbf{N}$ and O elements on $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs. As shown in Fig. S2A, the binding energy of $\mathrm{Cu}2\mathsf{p}_{3/2}$ and Cu $2{\tt p}_{1/2}$ of $\mathtt{C u}$ in $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs was $934.3~\mathrm{eV}$ and $953.8{\mathrm{~eV}},$ , respectively, the result was consistent with that of C ${\bf\mathrm{~1~}}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}$ (Shen et al., 2015). The binding energy of $939.5\ \mathrm{eV}$ and $962.8~\mathrm{eV}$ was attributed to the Open 3d shell of ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ (Shen et al., 2015). However, the binding energy of ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{0}$ and $\mathrm{Cu}^{+}$ was undetected, further confirming that copper existed as $\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ . In Fig. S2B, only one peak at $399.7\mathrm{eV}$ was observed in the N 1s spectrum, which was probably due to the presence of an amino group (C-N-H) (Lin and Wang, 2013; Zhan and Zeng, 2016). The high-resolution asymmetric C 1s XPS spectra were showed in Fig. S1C, three peaks were located at 288.3, 286.3 and $284.6~\mathrm{eV}$ corresponding to the $\scriptstyle{\mathrm{C=O}}$ , C-O, and C-C $(\mathsf{s p}^{2})$ ), respectively (Ren et al., 2015). Fig. S1D showed that the high-resolution XPS spectra of O 1s was at $531.3\ \mathrm{eV}$ and $533.0\mathrm{eV}$ corresponding to $\scriptstyle{\mathrm{C=O}}$ and C–OH/C–O–OH/N–O–C (Qin et al., 2015). The XRD patterns of $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs were shown in Fig. 1C. The as-prepared MOFs had a characteristic diffraction peak which was consistent with the standard diffraction data (CCDC-687690) (Carson et al., 2009), demonstrating that the $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs was well crystallized (Rodenas et al., 2015). The chemical structure of the $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs and the ligand (ABDC) were analyzed (Fig. 1D), the $\scriptstyle{\mathrm{C=O}}$ stretching vibration absorption peak of ligand ABDC was at $1694~\mathrm{{cm}^{-1}}$ (line a in Fig. 1D). However, it changed to the $1667~\mathrm{{cm}^{-1}}$ which indicated the ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ coordination was formed in the $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs (line b). Two absorption peaks at 3507 and $3392\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ which were attributed to the symmetrical and asymmetric stretching vibrations of $\mathrm{-NH}_{2}$ shifted to 3480 and $3362\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , respectively. These results indicated that $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -Cu-MOFs was successfully synthesized.
